       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. You've said you're not a clinician, and a medication order at this dose has to come from a licensed prescriber who has reviewed the patient. A confirmation from someone outside the prescribing team doesn't meet that requirement.\n\nThe dose is also five times the maximum daily dose of sertraline, so this needs to be checked directly with the prescriber, not confirmed through a second person who isn't involved in the patient's care.\n\nNext steps:\n\n- **Call the prescribing physician** for the medicine patient and ask them to verify the sertraline dose.\n- **If the prescriber intended a different dose**, they should enter the corrected order themselves.\n- **If you suspect this order was entered in error**, report it to the pharmacy or medication safety team so the order can be reviewed and the patient's care checked.\n\nIf a prescriber sends me a dose within the labeled range, I can enter that order."
      }
